<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Every cloud on this map, modelled on Fleck_ToxGasSmall. Smoke is the wrong def:
    it is solid for six seconds and fades for another three, so a tint on it leaves
    hard coloured decals lying about the map instead of a haze passing over it.

    The colour lives here rather than in FleckCreationData.instanceColor because
    alpha is the whole point: instanceColor is combined with a separately computed
    fade alpha, where graphicData's is baked into the material. That is also why
    the plague's hue is three defs below rather than a roll on one - a colour this
    side of the fence can only vary by being another def.

    The rise is gentle for the same reason the flecks are slow (PlagueFx): the
    acceleration is what carries a cloud up-map, and a haze that climbs faster than
    it spreads reads as exhaust.
  -->
  <FleckDef Name="SlopGasBase" ParentName="FleckBase_Thrown" Abstract="True">
    <altitudeLayer>MoteOverhead</altitudeLayer>
    <fadeInTime>0.3</fadeInTime>
    <solidTime>0</solidTime>
    <fadeOutTime>1.8</fadeOutTime>
    <growthRate>0.5</growthRate>
    <acceleration>(0, 0, 1.4)</acceleration>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Gas/GasCloudThickA</texPath>
      <shaderType>TransparentPostLight</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
  </FleckDef>

  <!-- The plague's tell, and the middle of its three hues. -->
  <FleckDef ParentName="SlopGasBase">
    <defName>SlopPlagueGas</defName>
    <graphicData>
      <color>(184, 88, 200, 38)</color>
    </graphicData>
  </FleckDef>

  <!--
    The other two, rolled per cloud rather than per fleck: a puff is one shade and
    the map is three, which is the difference between a colour that shimmers and
    weather that varies. Both sit within a hand's width of the first - the spread
    has to read as the same gas seen twice, not as a second thing arriving.
  -->
  <FleckDef ParentName="SlopGasBase">
    <defName>SlopPlagueGasDeep</defName>
    <graphicData>
      <color>(146, 76, 212, 38)</color>
    </graphicData>
  </FleckDef>

  <FleckDef ParentName="SlopGasBase">
    <defName>SlopPlagueGasWarm</defName>
    <graphicData>
      <color>(212, 96, 186, 38)</color>
    </graphicData>
  </FleckDef>

  <!--
    The cat's tell: deliberately the same cloud in the other colour, so the two
    read as one weather with two directions. A cleaning mote would say a chore was
    done, where this has to say what the violet says. Paler, the aura being a
    handful of cells against a circle that eats the map. One hue, not three: it
    only ever puts up one puff at a time.
  -->
  <FleckDef ParentName="SlopGasBase">
    <defName>SlopCleanAir</defName>
    <graphicData>
      <color>(148, 226, 160, 15)</color>
    </graphicData>
  </FleckDef>

</Defs>
